BE-300 2.6.8.1: build with the Debian/Ubuntu GCC 10.3 + binutils + make 4.3.

  * Top-level CFLAGS: -fgnu89-inline (C99 inline emitted duplicate
    out-of-line copies of header inlines), no stack protector / PIE,
    -fno-delete-null-pointer-checks, -fno-strict-overflow,
    -fno-tree-loop-distribute-patterns, plus warning classes the 2004
    sources trip everywhere.
  * uaccess.h: get_user() no longer casts its lvalue (cast-as-lvalue) and
    its asm output temporary is a plain long/long long, not a possibly
    const typeof(*ptr).
  * HI/LO: the "h"/"l" asm constraints and the "accum" clobber are gone
    from GCC; time.c, delay.h and div64.h use C for the high word.
  * sim.h save_static_function(): tail-jump explicitly into _sys_<name>
    and mark the bodies used/noinline/noclone.  The wrappers used to fall
    through into whatever C function followed; GCC 10 reorders functions,
    so kernel_thread()'s clone landed in sys_pipe (same fix as 2.4).
  * pg-r4k.c: clear_page/copy_page buffers defined in asm (GCC refuses a
    function alias of an array).
  * scall32-o32.S: .purgem before redefining the `sys' macro.
  * vmlinux.lds is generated as vmlinux.lds (new %.lds: %.lds.S rule):
    the old vmlinux.lds.s output overwrote vmlinux.lds.S on a
    case-insensitive host file system.
  * arch/mips/lib/gcc-helpers.c: __ashldi3/__ashrdi3/__lshrdi3 and an
    out-of-line strcpy, which GCC 10 calls on its own (no libgcc).
  * include/linux/init.h: define early_initcall(); kernel.org 2.6.8.1
    reserved .initcall.early1.init but never defined the macro, so board
    hooks such as vr41xx_pmu_init silently became implicit declarations.
  * Small C fixes: giu.c cascade irqaction declared before use, a block
    scope static prototype in prio_tree.c, vesa_modes declared after
    struct fb_videomode, mconf.c's shadowed current_menu.

